Let the DRM switch actually fetch the CDM, for the one component it needs.

Reported on Linux: a player says "failed to init media keys for EME", and a
test page reports only org.w3.clearkey with security level none. That is a
browser with no Widevine CDM at all, and it is what every Aerium desktop build
has been. The switch added by aerium-drm-media.patch could never do anything.

Read out of the 152 sources rather than assumed:

  enable_widevine=true comes from ungoogled-chromium's flags.gn, so the EME
  plumbing is compiled and the key system looks like it exists.

  bundle_widevine_cdm is enable_library_widevine_cdm && (is_chrome_branded ||
  is_chrome_for_testing_branded) in third_party/widevine/cdm/widevine.gni.
  Aerium is neither, so it is false and GetBundledWidevine() is not compiled.

  enable_widevine_cdm_component is computed, not a build argument, and is true
  for us - so GetHintedWidevine() IS compiled. It reads a hint file that only
  Component Updater writes.

  Component Updater cannot write it. component_updater_url_constants.cc is in
  ungoogled-chromium's domain_substitution.list, and the regex
  google([A-Za-z\-]*?\\*?)\.com rewrites update.googleapis.com to a host that
  does not resolve.

So AddWidevine() falls through to its own "Widevine enabled but no library
found" and registers nothing, leaving ClearKey - which is built into Chromium
and needs no CDM - as the only key system. That is exactly the report.

The fix is to let the component do its job, because the component is already
the right answer. It fetches over the update protocol, verifies the CRX3
signature, unpacks, and then either calls UpdateWidevineCdmHintFile() on Linux
or CdmRegistry::RegisterCdm() directly everywhere else - so this covers Windows
as well, and covers it without a restart, since that path registers at runtime.
Writing a downloader by hand would have meant reimplementing signature
verification for a binary that gets dlopen'd, which is not a thing to hand-roll.

There is no simpler source to fetch from. The dl.google.com/widevine-cdm bucket
that older helper scripts use is gone: versions.txt and every version-specific
zip return 404 now. The update service is what is left.

Two changes, in two files chosen because neither is in domain_substitution.list
- checked, not assumed - and apply_patches runs before apply_domsub in
scripts/build.sh, so a real hostname written in them survives:

  ChromeConfigurator::UpdateUrl() returns the real service when the switch is
  on, and upstream's rewritten one when it is not.

  RegisterComponentsForUpdate() registers the Widevine CDM component and
  returns, so it is the only component registered at all.

That second half is what keeps this honest. UpdateUrl() belongs to the
configurator rather than to a component, so a real URL is a real URL for
everything registered against it. Registering nothing else means there is
nothing else to ask about. Nothing is lost by skipping them: with the switch
off they are all pointed at the rewritten host already, so they have never
updated in this browser and they do not begin to now.

Stated plainly, because the switch now means more than it did: turning DRM on
contacts Google's update service. It asks for one component and downloads one
thing. The string under the switch says so.

Off by default, unchanged. PingUrl() is deliberately left rewritten - pings are
telemetry, a failed ping is non-fatal to the update flow, and fetching a CDM
does not need one.

Verified by applying this to the real 152.0.7977.82 registration.cc and
chrome_component_updater_configurator.cc with the same flags build.py uses:
both hunks land, and the result reads back correct. The hunks were generated
with git diff against those files rather than counted by hand.

--- a/chrome/browser/component_updater/chrome_component_updater_configurator.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/component_updater/chrome_component_updater_configurator.cc
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <vector>
 
 #include "base/check.h"
+#include "base/command_line.h"
 #include "base/files/file_path.h"
 #include "base/functional/bind.h"
 #include "base/functional/callback.h"
@@ -161,6 +162,22 @@ base::TimeDelta ChromeConfigurator::UpdateDelay() const {
 
 std::vector<GURL> ChromeConfigurator::UpdateUrl() const {
   DCHECK_CALLED_ON_VALID_SEQUENCE(sequence_checker_);
+  // Aerium: the real update service, and only when the user has switched DRM
+  // on. This file is not in ungoogled-chromium's domain_substitution.list, so
+  // the host written here survives apply_domsub - which runs after
+  // apply_patches in scripts/build.sh - where the same string in
+  // component_updater_url_constants.cc does not. That rewrite is why the
+  // Widevine CDM component has never been able to download anything, and it
+  // stays in force for every other build of this browser.
+  //
+  // Reached only with exactly one component registered; see
+  // RegisterComponentsForUpdate() in registration.cc for why that matters.
+  // PingUrl() is deliberately left rewritten: pings are telemetry, the update
+  // flow treats a failed ping as non-fatal, and nothing about fetching a CDM
+  // needs one.
+  if (base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch("enable-widevine")) {
+    return {GURL("https://update.googleapis.com/service/update2/json")};
+  }
   return configurator_impl_.UpdateUrl();
 }
 
--- a/chrome/browser/component_updater/registration.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/component_updater/registration.cc
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/component_updater/registration.h"
 
 #include "base/feature_list.h"
+#include "base/command_line.h"
 #include "base/files/file_path.h"
 #include "base/files/file_util.h"
 #include "base/functional/bind.h"
@@ -139,6 +140,28 @@ void DeleteOldComponents(const base::FilePath& user_data_dir) {
 void RegisterComponentsForUpdate() {
   auto* const cus = g_browser_process->component_updater();
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_WIDEVINE_CDM_COMPONENT)
+  // Aerium: when DRM is switched on, the Widevine CDM component is the ONLY
+  // component registered, and this returns before reaching any other.
+  //
+  // That narrowness is the whole point. ChromeConfigurator::UpdateUrl() is a
+  // property of the configurator, not of a component, so pointing it at the
+  // real update service to fetch the CDM points every registered component at
+  // it too. Registering nothing else means there is nothing else to fetch:
+  // turning on DRM asks Google for one thing, the CDM, and not for a list of
+  // everything else this browser could be told about.
+  //
+  // Nothing is lost by skipping them. ungoogled-chromium has
+  // component_updater_url_constants.cc in domain_substitution.list, so with
+  // the switch off every component below is already registered against a
+  // rewritten host that does not resolve. They have never updated in this
+  // browser and they do not start now.
+  if (base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch("enable-widevine")) {
+    RegisterWidevineCdmComponent(cus);
+    return;
+  }
+#endif  // BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_WIDEVINE_CDM_COMPONENT)
+
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
   RegisterRecoveryImprovedComponent(cus, g_browser_process->local_state());
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
